  {
    "id": "biographical_jack_ruby",
    "question": "Who was Jack Ruby?",
    "category": "biographical",
    "query_type_seen": "simple",
    "answer": "**Jack Ruby was a Dallas nightclub owner who shot and killed Lee Harvey Oswald, the alleged assassin of President John F. Kennedy.**\n\n- Ruby was described as having “substantial ties to the Mafia” and was involved in gambling and narcotics activities [1].\n- The Warren Commission recorded that Ruby drove a woman friend to the H.L. Hunt Oil Company offices in Dallas on the afternoon of November 21, 1963, the day before the assassination [2][3].\n- FBI records show that Special Agent Charles N. Flynn contacted Ruby in March 1959 to determine whether he possessed knowledge of criminal elements in Dallas; Ruby expressed willingness to provide information, but no useful intelligence was obtained [4].",
