  {
    "id": "biographical_oswald",
    "question": "Who was Lee Harvey Oswald?",
    "category": "biographical",
    "query_type_seen": "simple",
    "answer": "**Lee Harvey Oswald was a former United States Marine who later became a suspect in the assassination of President John F. Kennedy.**\n\n- He was born in New Orleans on October 18, 1939, and his Social Security number was 433‑54‑3937[2].  \n- He served in the U.S. Marine Corps from 24 Oct 1956 to 11 Sept 1959, bearing service number 1653230, and received an “undesirable” discharge on 13 Sept 1960[2][3].  \n- During his Marine service he held a “confidential” security clearance, as noted by a fellow Marine who supervised him[4].  \n- CIA records state that Oswald was never an informant or directly connected with the Agency, and the number 110669 cited in other contexts does not refer to him[1].",
